From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:25:21 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 30/39] Metal diamond engine: three dispatches per block
 (snapshot cg30b)

A mountain x valley tile reads mountain x mountain cells and its own, a valley x mountain tile the same, and no cell
is in both kinds within a block (a cell leaves its x mountain or its y mountain first), so the two phases do not
depend on each other and go in one dispatch: the tile set is the z index of the threadgroup, and the four tile
arrays are bound once per command buffer (OPENEMS_DIAMOND_MERGE=0: four dispatches). In paired rounds on a loaded
machine the GCPW line (0.24 M cells) ran 5-6 % faster and the notch tutorial about 10 %; nothing on 5 M cells.
diamond_check.sh 72 of 72 identical, twice.

